    "keccak_permutations": 129,
    "keccak": "Derived from the table and from the sources of sha3 0.10.9, not a figure that the node prints: the sha3 crate runs 129 Keccak-f[1600] permutations for one verification of the client's message. 96 for the 16 entries of A (each: 1 to absorb the seed, 5 for the 5 output blocks; the reader of sha3 runs a permutation after every block it returns, so the fifth is not used), 11 for tr, 12 for mu, 2 for the challenge, 8 for the last hash; 20 of the 129 follow the last block that is read. tr costs 127,555 units for its 11 permutations, about 11,600 each (the round loop of keccak_p is 475 instructions in 476 eight-byte slots, 24 rounds), so the permutations take about 1.50 million units, more than the 1,400,000 that a transaction may ask for; everything else (13 transforms, unpacking, products, hint) takes about 0.25 million."
  },
